Step 1 — Create project
mkdir fmcg-mcp
cd fmcg-mcp
npm init -y
npm pkg set type=module
npm install @modelcontextprotocol/server zod tsx
mkdir src
The current TypeScript SDK v2 quickstart uses Node.js 20+, ESM, @modelcontextprotocol/server, zod and tsx.

###########################
Step 2 — src/index.ts
import { McpServer } from "@modelcontextprotocol/server";
import { serveStdio } from "@modelcontextprotocol/server/stdio";
import * as z from "zod/v4";
const server = new McpServer({
 name: "fmcg-demo",
 version: "1.0.0",
});
server.registerTool(
 "get_product_sales",
 {
 title: "Get Product Sales",
 description: "Return synthetic sales for a product and region.",
 inputSchema: {
 product: z.string().min(1),
 region: z.string().min(1),
 },
 },
 async ({ product, region }) => ({
 content: [{
 type: "text",
 text: JSON.stringify({
 product,
 region,
 unitsSold: 12500,
 revenue: 875000
 })
 }]
 })
);
void serveStdio(() => server);
console.error("FMCG MCP server running");


